Benchmarks of the reentrant runtime (TXSERIES-PLAN.md, T1.7)

compare.sh BUILD_A BUILD_B [N]
    run time of single-thread programs with two builds (for example the
    runtime before the reentrant work and the current one):
    arith  arithmetic on DISPLAY, COMP-3 and COMP-5 fields
    strs   MOVE, STRING, INSPECT
    calls  dynamic CALL of a small program (csub)
    seqf   LINE SEQUENTIAL file, write and read
    idxf   INDEXED file, write and random read

scale.sh BUILD [CPUS]
    multi-thread scaling: each thread creates its own context and calls
    'work' (arithmetic, intrinsic functions, STRING, INSPECT, dynamic
    CALL of 'wsub') 300000 times.

The builds should be configured with CFLAGS=-O2, without --enable-debug.
Results of 2026-11-07 are in TXSERIES-PLAN.md (T1.7).
